...and it feels great!

Just a couple of weeks ago I got to the planes for the first time with a
healer, and now I finally did it with a rogue. I hadn't even completed the
rogue quest before. In your face, RNG!

The recipe to ascension is simply to have a bit of luck, not to be burdened,
and not to die stupidly. Most of my stupid deaths have been caused by
choking on food, hitting a floating eye and having been beaten to death by a
horde of rothes or something similar, and so on.

The ascension was easier than I thought. I just recently read the Endgame
spoiler which tells exactly what to do, where and when. Is it really
possible to finish the game without reading the spoilers? I mean how can one
know what is needed to get to the Moloch's Sanctum? Fortune cookies?

Anyway, here's the story of my rogue:

I started the game by relying on daggers for a change and couldn't believe
how easy it was to kill something like a mumak by throwing multiple daggers
in one shot.

On the second level I found an altar. No matter how much I offered monsters
I really got only things like Ogresmasher, Trollsbane, Sting and Werebane,
and of these I really only used the werebane, to get sabre experience for
later on. The rest of the artifacts were rather useless.

I found a wand of wishing on the fifth level and I got me a nice gray dragon
scale mail, but that's about it. I wished twice for a Frost Brand, but got
nothing, apparently because of those artifacts already created. Argh!
And because I hadn't identified the charge of the WoW, I zapped it for the
fourth time to check whether it should be recharged and of course with my
luck I wrested the last wish out of it. Argh! (I already had a blessed
charging scroll)

At this point I really thought about quitting the game.

Finally after some serious offering at the altar and a prayer I got
Stormbringer, which I held to the end. Not a bad artifact in the end,
because it gave level drain resistance, and Vampires & Wraiths were abundant
towards the end of the game and only a few creatures resist the level drain
attack. Then again I attacked several co-aligned unicorns and a priest...

So, I finished the mines and Sokoban easily with the Stormy, as well the
quest which was rather easy (after reading the rogue quest how-to!). I
really didn't use the Master Key of Thievery in the game for anything else
than opening doors and chests, and to counter the teleport attack of Q's.

I genocided at some point L's and h's for obvious reasons before the castle
and used the wishes from the castles's WoW to get a magic marker (the only
one in the game!), Gauntlets of Dex and something else. Can't remember.

I got back up, finished the Ludios founding nothing useful there, got back
down to Gehennom. I died one because of a cockatrice and put on the "oLS
just in time as I had nothing else the cancel the stoning! Right after this
I genocided all c's! I also at one point started to turn to green slime but
fortunately I had the /fire. So I got the amulet, went through the planes
quite easy and the middle altar was the right one, after I first toured the
left altar. The endgame riders are rather easy and should be hardened. Death
died in one or two hits which is not what I should expect from someone whose
name is "Death" and who gets a special mention in the Bible...

My only regrets were that I forgot the guardian angel and it was just a step
away to ascend with me...

